---
title: Connect your GitHub
description: The verified identity your course is attributed to. Required to submit the proposal.
sidebar:
  order: 3
---

Your course lives and gets reviewed on GitHub, so before submitting it you have to connect a verified GitHub identity. That's the **GitHub attribution** block in your instructor space.

## When it's needed

Only when you **submit** the proposal. You can create your instructor account, fill in your profile and write the whole course without GitHub connected.

## How to connect it

{% steps %}

1. In your instructor space, press **Connect GitHub**.

2. Authorise the connection on GitHub.

3. You come back with a verified identity and the block marked as completed.

{% /steps %}

## Decide the name before connecting

This is where you choose the name you appear under publicly as the course author. If you'd rather use a pseudonym, [create a GitHub account](https://github.com/signup) without your real name **before** connecting it.

## If that account was already in use

If the GitHub you connect already belongs to a profile associated with another Authentik account, the connection won't happen by itself: sign in with that other account, or ask support to verify both are yours. If what we find is an earlier profile of *yours*, we take you to the [recovery process](/en/profesores/perfil/#if-you-had-a-profile-before).
